1
00:01:48,079 --> 00:01:49,239
Chief Tan, you're awake.

2
00:01:51,439 --> 00:01:52,319
How long was I asleep?

3
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:54,920
Over an hour, I think.

4
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:57,920
Chief Tan, you stayed up late again.

5
00:02:00,799 --> 00:02:03,599
I was writing that PR material for Economic Crime.

6
00:02:03,799 --> 00:02:06,280
Worked on it until past 3:00 a.m.

7
00:02:08,439 --> 00:02:11,199
Chief Tan, you push yourself too hard.

8
00:02:12,599 --> 00:02:14,439
In my position,

9
00:02:15,159 --> 00:02:17,039
I have responsibilities to shoulder.

10
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:21,319
Chief Tan, your phone was vibrating earlier.

11
00:02:29,639 --> 00:02:30,039
Lao Na.

12
00:02:30,159 --> 00:02:30,800
Where are you?

13
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:31,520
What's the situation over there?

14
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:32,879
We're getting ready to close the net.

15
00:02:34,159 --> 00:02:35,560
Don't. I'll be there in ten minutes.

16
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,280
Wait for me. Wait!

17
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:38,319
Hurry, hurry!

18
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:42,759
Xiao Qu, grab the gear.

19
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:44,599
Lao Na.

20
00:02:45,479 --> 00:02:46,360
Why did you move in first?

21
00:02:46,599 --> 00:02:47,759
The targets showed up.

22
00:02:47,759 --> 00:02:48,680
How could we not grab them?

23
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:49,919
Why didn't you get here earlier?

24
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:50,759
There was traffic.

25
00:02:51,199 --> 00:02:51,599
Tell you what.

26
00:02:52,319 --> 00:02:52,960
Have the guys

27
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:53,879
cooperate a bit.

28
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:54,919
Let me shoot some details.

29
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,520
Quit messing around.

30
00:02:56,879 --> 00:02:58,039
You think we're shooting a movie?

31
00:02:58,639 --> 00:02:59,360
I'm not messing around.

32
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:00,000
Come on, follow me.

33
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,120
This case,

34
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:03,520
Provincial Director Liu takes it seriously.

35
00:03:04,319 --> 00:03:05,719
If I don't get firsthand footage,

36
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,199
it's a major failure.

37
00:03:07,719 --> 00:03:08,680
Shoot, come on!

38
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,400
Take another shot.

39
00:03:09,759 --> 00:03:10,520
Get some footage.

40
00:03:11,039 --> 00:03:12,120
I really can't help you with this.

41
00:03:12,639 --> 00:03:13,560
Anything else is fine,

42
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,280
but not this.

43
00:03:14,439 --> 00:03:15,719
Look, come back to the station with me,

44
00:03:15,719 --> 00:03:16,719
and we can just film the interrogation.

45
00:03:17,719 --> 00:03:18,039
Lao Na.

46
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:22,520
Then let me shoot some footage

47
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,639
of your stakeout and vehicle checks,

48
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:24,560
okay?

49
00:03:26,319 --> 00:03:27,120
The checkpoints are already cleared.

50
00:03:31,439 --> 00:03:32,280
Restore the checkpoint.

51
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:33,680
Thank you.

52
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,000
It's all for the job.

53
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:36,080
Not happening.

54
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:37,639
Captain Liao.

55
00:03:38,719 --> 00:03:39,479
Deputy Director Tan.

56
00:03:40,879 --> 00:03:42,039
We're not actors.

57
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,680
Much less extras.

58
00:03:44,719 --> 00:03:45,919
Captain Liao, you misunderstand.

59
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:48,759
The higher-ups are taking this seriously.

60
00:03:48,759 --> 00:03:49,479
We in SWAT...

61
00:03:50,439 --> 00:03:51,719
...don't do this superficial nonsense.

62
00:03:53,039 --> 00:03:55,039
Next time we have a drill, I'll let you know in advance.

63
00:03:55,039 --> 00:03:55,719
You can come film it properly.

64
00:03:57,599 --> 00:03:58,240
Get ready.

65
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:58,479
Ready.

66
00:03:58,599 --> 00:03:59,560
What is Liao Bufan's problem?

67
00:03:59,879 --> 00:04:00,759
Who is he mocking?

68
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,840
If I hadn't been at the night market...

69
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,479
...he'd have been disciplined long ago.

70
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:05,360
Exactly, exactly.

71
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,520
What an attitude.

72
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,000
Lao Lu.

73
00:04:08,719 --> 00:04:09,879
I'm in a rush to pick up a package.

74
00:04:09,919 --> 00:04:10,199
Hurry up.

75
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:16,079
M-Mainly, it's about not delaying training.

76
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:17,920
Chief Tan, look...

77
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:19,720
Today's arrest shoot...

78
00:04:20,079 --> 00:04:21,040
...doesn't feature the SWAT team...

79
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:22,199
...so nothing gets delayed.

80
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:22,920
Tell you what.

81
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,240
Coming.

82
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:25,879
Call us anytime you need help.

83
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:26,959
We will fully cooperate.

84
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:27,720
Let's begin.

85
00:04:28,319 --> 00:04:28,839
Set up the cameras.

86
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:29,639
Get a wide shot first.

87
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,480
This Liao Bufan from SWAT...

88
00:04:35,199 --> 00:04:36,160
...is completely undisciplined.

89
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:38,759
This guy in the brown shirt...

90
00:04:38,759 --> 00:04:39,879
...why does he keep looking at the camera?

91
00:04:40,319 --> 00:04:40,959
Have a word with him.

92
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,839
First time being filmed, he's nervous.

93
00:04:45,439 --> 00:04:46,240
Da Long, Da Long.

94
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,759
Why are you so nervous?

95
00:04:48,319 --> 00:04:49,759
Just act like you normally do.

96
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:51,480
Pretend they aren't here.

97
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:53,439
Got it, got it.

98
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:56,199
Alright, Xiao Qu, next vehicle.

99
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,040
That should be enough.

100
00:04:59,439 --> 00:05:00,199
One last vehicle.

101
00:05:01,399 --> 00:05:02,160
One last car, one last car.

102
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,879
Xiao Qu, get that minibus, hurry.

103
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:13,800
Driver's license and ID.

104
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,560
Please show your ID.

105
00:05:15,439 --> 00:05:15,959
Police inspection.

106
00:05:15,959 --> 00:05:16,879
Please show your ID card.

107
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:18,560
Look up.

108
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:23,879
What the...

109
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:27,079
Why is it fine if they look at the camera?

110
00:05:27,079 --> 00:05:27,399
Them?

111
00:05:28,399 --> 00:05:28,879
It's fine.

112
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:31,120
They're civilians, it's normal to look.

113
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,639
You can't dictate where they look.

114
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:35,240
Keep your eyes on the subjects.

115
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:41,000
Hello, please show your ID.

116
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:46,560
No, look.

117
00:05:47,439 --> 00:05:49,399
This guy isn't looking either, right?

118
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,240
Realism... we need realism.

119
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:54,360
Da Long, Da Long!

120
00:05:54,839 --> 00:05:56,360
That guy in the hat is suspicious.

121
00:05:56,399 --> 00:05:56,759
Restrain him!

122
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:02,639
What problem?

123
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,560
Hold him down! Hold him!

124
00:06:05,759 --> 00:06:06,199
Turn him over.

125
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:06,839
Xiao Qu!

126
00:06:07,399 --> 00:06:08,600
Don't move! Don't move! Freeze!

127
00:06:08,839 --> 00:06:09,279
Don't move!

128
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:09,800
Stay still!

129
00:06:10,199 --> 00:06:10,519
Xiao Qu!

130
00:06:10,519 --> 00:06:10,959
Turn him over!

131
00:06:11,519 --> 00:06:12,639
Xiao Qu, are you filming?

132
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:13,759
I'm rolling.

133
00:06:13,959 --> 00:06:14,639
Not missing a single frame.

134
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:17,680
What is this?

135
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:19,360
Milk powder.

136
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,000
Get up.

137
00:06:23,839 --> 00:06:24,600
Let's shoot some close-ups.

138
00:06:25,519 --> 00:06:25,879
Don't block the camera!

139
00:06:25,879 --> 00:06:26,680
Hurry and call me an ambulance!

140
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:27,240
Don't block the camera!

141
00:06:27,279 --> 00:06:27,800
My leg is broken!

142
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,560
Okay, okay, okay.

143
00:06:45,519 --> 00:06:47,279
Lang Tao, going in circles is pointless.

144
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:47,839
Alright.

145
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,560
It's your leg that's injured.

146
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:51,680
Not your head.

147
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,279
Where did this shipment come from?

148
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:55,639
Where were you going to send it?

149
00:07:13,439 --> 00:07:14,040
I'm

150
00:07:17,759 --> 00:07:18,240
thirsty.

151
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:39,160
Thanks.

152
00:07:44,879 --> 00:07:45,920
I'm telling you, Lin Nan,

153
00:07:46,399 --> 00:07:48,199
when I watched the footage,

154
00:07:48,199 --> 00:07:49,759
I knew something was off with this guy.

155
00:07:51,639 --> 00:07:52,439
And sure enough,

156
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:54,600
we caught him red-handed.

157
00:07:55,439 --> 00:07:56,319
Was it drugs?

158
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,160
Definitely.

159
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:00,120
Nice work.

160
00:08:01,319 --> 00:08:01,759
Where's Lao Na?

161
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:04,079
He's doing the handover with Lao Zhang.

162
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,639
He's here. I'm hanging up.

163
00:08:08,839 --> 00:08:09,519
Was it drugs?

164
00:08:09,519 --> 00:08:10,920
Why haven't you headed back yet?

165
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:12,199
I was afraid you'd starve.

166
00:08:15,639 --> 00:08:17,000
I'm asking you. Was it drugs?

167
00:08:21,079 --> 00:08:21,720
Well,

168
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:25,040
you'll have to ask Zhang Peng.

169
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:25,959
I'm not in Narcotics.

170
00:08:28,519 --> 00:08:29,680
It's at least a kilo, right?

171
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:35,840
All I can tell you is,

172
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:37,840
it's quite a large amount.

173
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:44,600
You really owe me a thank you for this.

174
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,240
If it weren't for me...

175
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:47,399
Chief Guo.

176
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:49,600
About what happened today...

177
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,039
I... I was right there at the scene.

178
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:52,799
I filmed the entire process.

179
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,200
I've heard all about what happened today.

180
00:08:55,559 --> 00:08:55,879
Haitao.

181
00:08:56,519 --> 00:08:57,639
Organize your men immediately

182
00:08:57,919 --> 00:08:58,960
and hold a meeting with Narcotics.

183
00:09:00,799 --> 00:09:02,600
Chief Guo, do you need Publicity Section

184
00:09:02,919 --> 00:09:04,519
to film and record the meeting?

185
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:05,679
No, that won't be necessary.

186
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:07,039
What are you eating?

187
00:09:07,279 --> 00:09:08,440
Burgers. Want one? We have some.

188
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:09,159
Is there one for me?

189
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:10,639
He took it.

190
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:12,399
Never mind.

191
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:14,960
We still have coffee.

192
00:09:15,279 --> 00:09:16,039
I'll take a coffee then.

193
00:09:16,039 --> 00:09:16,320
Coffee.

194
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:19,639
Thanks.

195
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,639
The drugs seized this time

196
00:09:33,919 --> 00:09:34,960
totaled two kilograms.

197
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:36,799
After testing,

198
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:37,919
the composition of this drug

199
00:09:38,279 --> 00:09:39,480
is identical to that of

200
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:41,960
the new drug "Spring Snow" seized

201
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,639
in other provinces.

202
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,519
Setting aside the fake "Spring Snow"

203
00:09:44,519 --> 00:09:45,480
we seized previously,

204
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,080
this is the first time

205
00:09:47,279 --> 00:09:49,080
this new drug has appeared in Hongye City.

206
00:09:52,279 --> 00:09:53,320
What's the suspect's status?

207
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,320
Broken leg. Handcuffed at the hospital.

208
00:09:59,399 --> 00:09:59,879
A broken leg?

209
00:10:02,159 --> 00:10:03,600
Hey, don't look at me.

210
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:04,639
I didn't do anything.

211
00:10:05,159 --> 00:10:06,840
He broke it himself when he jumped from the car.

212
00:10:07,039 --> 00:10:08,000
The guys from the Publicity Section

213
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,039
filmed the whole thing.

214
00:10:09,679 --> 00:10:10,440
Speaking of the Publicity Section,

215
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:12,080
I think Tan Yan

216
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:13,720
made a major contribution, didn't he?

217
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:14,840
Right. If it weren't for him,

218
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:15,840
our operation this time...

219
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:17,080
What did the suspect confess?

220
00:10:17,559 --> 00:10:19,399
Did he reveal the source of the drugs?

221
00:10:21,159 --> 00:10:21,799
He didn't say a word.

222
00:10:21,799 --> 00:10:23,919
He probably knows he's in deep trouble,

223
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:24,600
so he's just holding out.

224
00:10:26,919 --> 00:10:27,399
Keep interrogating him.

225
00:10:28,399 --> 00:10:29,320
We need to make him talk.

226
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,039
Yes, sir.

227
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:00,399
Hungry?

228
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,120
All good stuff.

229
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:10,799
Here's some chicken.

230
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:12,679
Here are the veggies.

231
00:11:13,799 --> 00:11:14,200
And liquor.

232
00:11:15,399 --> 00:11:16,320
Any news?

233
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,360
I'm... I'm looking.

234
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:23,960
Even though you only gave me one photo,

235
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,039
but trust me,

236
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:26,360
I... I have what it takes.

237
00:11:28,919 --> 00:11:29,120
I do.

238
00:11:31,639 --> 00:11:32,120
Come play a hand.

239
00:11:37,679 --> 00:11:38,879
Play? Play what?

240
00:11:38,879 --> 00:11:40,399
Play what? Aren't I looking for your guy!

241
00:11:40,399 --> 00:11:41,399
I'm still looking for him.

242
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:42,879
I'm helping you find someone!

243
00:11:46,759 --> 00:11:47,399
Another Bamboo.

244
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,080
Play it.

245
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,360
Play, hurry up.

246
00:11:49,639 --> 00:11:50,440
Two of Bamboo. Pass.

247
00:11:50,519 --> 00:11:51,200
So slow.

248
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:54,200
Eight of Dots.

249
00:11:56,919 --> 00:11:57,799
Full flush, straight.

250
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,919
Pay up, pay up, pay up, pay up!

251
00:12:00,799 --> 00:12:02,159
Come on, pay up.

252
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:03,559
I'm not playing, not playing, not playing.

253
00:12:04,639 --> 00:12:05,639
I'll owe you for now.

254
00:12:06,159 --> 00:12:07,320
You haven't even paid for last time.

255
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,639
Let me owe you one more time.

256
00:12:08,919 --> 00:12:10,120
Alright, alright. Come on.

257
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:10,759
Let's keep going.

258
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,919
You really suck at this game.

259
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:14,159
Taking my cigarettes again.

260
00:12:14,279 --> 00:12:15,080
I'll buy you some tomorrow.

261
00:13:00,879 --> 00:13:02,159
Sis, uh, I'm eating out.

262
00:13:02,159 --> 00:13:02,879
Having dinner with friends.

263
00:13:02,879 --> 00:13:03,639
I'll be home in a bit.

264
00:13:03,639 --> 00:13:04,240
I didn't do anything.

265
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,279
I'm hanging up. Hanging up.

266
00:13:08,279 --> 00:13:09,360
I'm hanging up, Sis. Hanging up.

267
00:14:18,159 --> 00:14:18,799
Okay, no problem.

268
00:14:18,919 --> 00:14:19,159
Go ahead.

269
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:19,440
Okay.

270
00:14:19,639 --> 00:14:19,919
No problem.

271
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:22,039
Zhi.

272
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:22,879
Chief Tan is here.

273
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:23,360
Morning.

274
00:14:25,799 --> 00:14:26,759
Up all night again, huh?

275
00:14:26,919 --> 00:14:27,519
You bet.

276
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:28,759
Caught a bunch of kids last night

277
00:14:28,759 --> 00:14:29,960
who were street racing.

278
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:31,799
Taking statements until what, 3 or 4 a.m.?

279
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,039
Crashed in the dorm for the night.

280
00:14:34,559 --> 00:14:35,559
Is Chief Ji still sleeping?

281
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,320
I wish.

282
00:14:36,559 --> 00:14:37,399
He's probably on his way back by now.

283
00:14:38,279 --> 00:14:39,159
Where did he go this time?

284
00:14:39,639 --> 00:14:42,080
Mr. Jin's son called first thing today.

285
00:14:42,159 --> 00:14:43,720
Said he's refusing to take his meds again.

286
00:14:44,279 --> 00:14:45,320
So the chief was called over there again.

287
00:14:45,639 --> 00:14:47,519
Why does your station have so much going on lately?

288
00:14:47,679 --> 00:14:49,240
You got me. I'm wondering the same thing.

289
00:14:49,679 --> 00:14:51,919
Someone loses a dog, another green onions,

290
00:14:51,919 --> 00:14:52,879
and they all come to us.

291
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,399
Our police PR work

292
00:14:56,399 --> 00:14:57,080
must be doing great.

293
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:57,720
Absolutely spot on.

294
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,039
"Call 110 for help"

295
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,360
has really sunk in.

296
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:00,879
Exactly.

297
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:04,440
Xiao Qu.

298
00:15:07,039 --> 00:15:07,399
What's up?

299
00:15:09,159 --> 00:15:09,679
Looking for me?

300
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:11,879
Did they say what it's about?

301
00:15:13,759 --> 00:15:14,320
Alright, be right there.

302
00:15:16,159 --> 00:15:16,879
Have you had breakfast?

303
00:15:17,159 --> 00:15:17,759
Haven't had the time.

304
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,279
Freshly fried dough. Don't let it get cold.

305
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:20,080
It won't taste good if it's cold.

306
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:20,679
Okay.

307
00:15:20,799 --> 00:15:21,080
Thanks, Chief Tan.

308
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:21,759
Share some with the team.

309
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:22,200
Will do.

310
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:24,000
Give this soy milk to Chief Ji.

311
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:25,279
Alright, I'll take it over right now.

312
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:26,360
Drive safe.

313
00:15:32,919 --> 00:15:35,840
Leaving Baidi amid the morning clouds,

314
00:15:37,399 --> 00:15:40,080
A thousand miles to Jiangling in a day.

315
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:44,039
While monkeys on both banks keep calling,

316
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,320
The light skiff

317
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:48,399
The light skiff

318
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,279
The skiff has passed ten thousand peaks.

319
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,159
The skiff has passed... It has passed...

320
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:02,879
Mr. Jin.

321
00:16:04,159 --> 00:16:05,720
Mr. Jin, class is over.

322
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,399
It's time to take your medicine.

323
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:09,480
I'm not sick, why would I take medicine?

324
00:16:10,799 --> 00:16:11,960
The skiff has passed.

325
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:13,919
The skiff has passed.

326
00:16:13,919 --> 00:16:14,919
He's been like this a lot lately.

327
00:16:15,919 --> 00:16:17,120
Locking the door at the drop of a hat,

328
00:16:17,279 --> 00:16:18,639
refusing to come out no matter what.

329
00:16:19,039 --> 00:16:20,000
He doesn't even recognize me anymore.

330
00:16:20,159 --> 00:16:21,360
And he keeps asking me where Gangzi went.

331
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,720
Couldn't you just take off the latch?

332
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:25,840
Mr. Jin.

333
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:27,600
Class is over. The bell rang.

334
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:28,720
Who are you?

335
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:31,080
I'm Xiao Min, your student.

336
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,159
I used to eat at your house as a kid.

337
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Xiao Min?

338
00:16:35,879 --> 00:16:37,120
What do you do now?

339
00:16:40,759 --> 00:16:41,679
I'm a police officer.

340
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:42,919
Police?

341
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,080
Did you guys arrest Gangzi?

342
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,159
Where did you take him?

343
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:52,519
Dad.

344
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:53,840
I'm right here.

345
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:54,759
I'm perfectly fine.

346
00:16:55,919 --> 00:16:56,559
Who are you?

347
00:16:57,639 --> 00:16:58,759
What are you supposed to be?

348
00:17:05,119 --> 00:17:05,720
Mr. Jin.

349
00:17:06,599 --> 00:17:08,160
Gangzi got involved with the wrong things.

350
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:10,599
The police arrested him to save him.

351
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:13,839
As long as he stays away from that stuff,

352
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:15,039
he'll be fine.

353
00:17:17,839 --> 00:17:19,839
Then when are you going to let him out?

354
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:21,799
Mr. Jin, you need to take your medicine first.

355
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,039
Here, like this, come on.

356
00:17:25,599 --> 00:17:26,279
If you take your medicine,

357
00:17:26,279 --> 00:17:27,799
I promise Gangzi will come back tonight.

358
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:28,240
Okay?

359
00:17:28,559 --> 00:17:28,839
Hand.

360
00:17:30,079 --> 00:17:30,799
You said so.

361
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:31,559
I did.

362
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:34,720
One white pill.

363
00:17:37,079 --> 00:17:39,079
If I take this, he'll be back tonight?

364
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:39,640
Take it.

365
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:40,279
Yes, he will.

366
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:53,480
Why do you look a bit familiar?

367
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:57,359
Familiar. Very familiar.

368
00:17:58,400 --> 00:17:58,920
Very.

369
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,839
About the Police Open Day...

370
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:08,920
It was assigned to Chief Zhao.

371
00:18:10,559 --> 00:18:11,519
I feel like Chief Guo originally wanted

372
00:18:11,519 --> 00:18:12,240
to assign it to you,

373
00:18:12,519 --> 00:18:13,440
but you weren't here.

374
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:15,720
Did Chief Guo say anything else?

375
00:18:17,039 --> 00:18:18,160
Nothing else really.

376
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:19,200
Oh, right.

377
00:18:19,519 --> 00:18:21,240
He asked if I was at the arrest scene too,

378
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:22,680
and called us lucky charms.

379
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:31,119
Chief Guo's ability to recognize people

380
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:32,160
is top-notch.

381
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:33,200
Chief Tan,

382
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:35,240
if they give out commendations later,

383
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:36,200
will we get a share of the credit?

384
00:18:37,359 --> 00:18:38,480
Comrade Xiao Qu,

385
00:18:39,599 --> 00:18:42,200
don't always think about that at work.

386
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:46,599
Even though we're on the publicity front,

387
00:18:47,559 --> 00:18:50,000
fighting crime

388
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,440
is also part of our job.

389
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:52,160
Chief Tan!

390
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:55,480
You didn't get hurt, did you?

391
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:56,720
No, I didn't.

392
00:18:59,440 --> 00:18:59,799
Really,

393
00:19:00,759 --> 00:19:02,200
that was amazing. Truly amazing!

394
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:03,279
What's so amazing?

395
00:19:03,599 --> 00:19:05,559
Many people called me this morning

396
00:19:05,599 --> 00:19:06,759
just to talk about what you did yesterday.

397
00:19:07,839 --> 00:19:08,839
Listening to them, I was truly

398
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:10,400
pumped up.

399
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:12,960
Who says we in publicity

400
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,000
can only wield pens?

401
00:19:14,519 --> 00:19:15,440
Even carrying cameras,

402
00:19:16,079 --> 00:19:16,960
we can still catch drug dealers!

403
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:19,079
Chief Zhao,

404
00:19:19,759 --> 00:19:20,640
your reminder

405
00:19:21,759 --> 00:19:22,920
warms my heart.

406
00:19:23,559 --> 00:19:26,400
I really couldn't control myself yesterday.

407
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:31,000
The golden shield

408
00:19:31,559 --> 00:19:32,319
is forged with passionate blood.

409
00:19:33,079 --> 00:19:35,000
You showed your skills in a crisis.

410
00:19:36,279 --> 00:19:37,960
As for me, now I can only

411
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:39,160
focus on doing my own job well.

412
00:19:39,839 --> 00:19:41,200
Chief Guo just gave me another task.

413
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:42,839
It's really stumped me.

414
00:19:45,759 --> 00:19:46,519
I... I wanted

415
00:19:46,519 --> 00:19:48,000
to get some advice from you on this.

416
00:19:49,119 --> 00:19:51,119
Last year, you and the traffic police

417
00:19:51,119 --> 00:19:51,759
organized that

418
00:19:51,799 --> 00:19:52,440
Open Day event.

419
00:19:52,839 --> 00:19:53,920
The feedback was great.

420
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:55,079
How... how did you manage it?

421
00:19:57,359 --> 00:19:58,039
It's not easy.

422
00:19:58,480 --> 00:19:59,839
Chief Zhao, it's really not easy.

423
00:20:00,759 --> 00:20:01,640
Let me warn you,

424
00:20:01,839 --> 00:20:03,000
it's going to be exhausting,

425
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,400
and you'll end up offending people.

426
00:20:06,519 --> 00:20:08,680
The public is tired of seeing police stations.

427
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:11,200
Seeing them all the time, there's no novelty.

428
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:14,720
CID, Econ Crime, Narcotics, Security...

429
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:17,559
they're too busy to cooperate.

430
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:18,720
Which is understandable.

431
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:20,839
Plus, there's a lot of classified info.

432
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:22,359
It's tough. Really tough.

433
00:20:23,079 --> 00:20:23,880
Yeah.

434
00:20:24,519 --> 00:20:24,920
I've been...

435
00:20:28,519 --> 00:20:29,680
I've been pondering this for a while.

436
00:20:31,799 --> 00:20:33,279
I want to do something different,

437
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:37,640
but I'm afraid of adding to everyone's burden.

438
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:40,920
It's quite a dilemma.

439
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:55,440
Deputy Director Tan, we're not actors.

440
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:56,920
And definitely not extras.

441
00:21:05,319 --> 00:21:05,799
Chief Zhao.

442
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:11,079
Do you think the SWAT team would be a good fit?

443
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:17,759
The SWAT team, huh?

444
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:21,240
Yeah. They mostly just train and patrol.

445
00:21:23,759 --> 00:21:24,680
The key is, their work isn't classified.

446
00:21:25,359 --> 00:21:26,480
And the public still finds them mysterious.

447
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:28,680
It's perfect!

448
00:21:30,079 --> 00:21:30,559
My goodness.

449
00:21:32,119 --> 00:21:33,279
Why didn't I think of that?

450
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:36,240
Chief Tan, you really are...

451
00:21:38,119 --> 00:21:39,880
Xiao Qu, learn from this.

452
00:21:40,559 --> 00:21:41,680
Look at Chief Tan's way of thinking.

453
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:43,440
His vision, his broad perspective.

454
00:21:44,039 --> 00:21:44,680
It really opened my eyes.

455
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,400
Then I'll go contact them right now.

456
00:21:48,319 --> 00:21:48,640
Xiao Qu, come on.

457
00:21:49,319 --> 00:21:50,480
Quick, give me a ride. Come on, let's go.

458
00:21:55,119 --> 00:21:56,920
The old timer underestimated them.

459
00:21:58,480 --> 00:21:59,440
The SWAT team...

460
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:02,119
is tough to deal with.

461
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,039
Let's get together this weekend.

462
00:22:09,640 --> 00:22:10,240
The usual place.

463
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:25,880
Hello, viewers.

464
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,839
We are live at the Police Open Day event.

465
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:29,680
As you can see, our SWAT officers

466
00:22:29,680 --> 00:22:31,680
are now performing a rappelling demonstration.

467
00:23:09,079 --> 00:23:09,400
Look at this.

468
00:23:10,039 --> 00:23:11,359
The public is very enthusiastic.

469
00:23:11,359 --> 00:23:13,039
It's very effective. Look.

470
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:15,359
The results are great.

471
00:23:17,079 --> 00:23:18,079
Thank you so much.

472
00:23:18,599 --> 00:23:19,400
Thank you, Captain Liao.

473
00:23:19,599 --> 00:23:20,160
Thank you, Commissar.

474
00:23:22,039 --> 00:23:24,519
We should be the ones thanking you.

475
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,319
This has given our SWAT team

476
00:23:26,519 --> 00:23:27,480
such great publicity.

477
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:30,079
Chief Zhao.

478
00:23:31,039 --> 00:23:32,400
How did you come up with the idea

479
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,960
to make our SWAT team

480
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:35,799
the theme of this police open day?

481
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:39,720
This was actually Chief Tan's idea.

482
00:23:39,720 --> 00:23:40,839
I wouldn't have dared to think of it myself.

483
00:23:42,279 --> 00:23:43,279
Yeah, the results are great.

484
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:45,319
Keep an eye on things.

485
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:47,880
Where are you going?

486
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:52,160
To the restroom.

487
00:23:56,839 --> 00:23:59,079
Chief Zhao, look how grand their courtyard is.

488
00:23:59,400 --> 00:23:59,759
Yeah.

489
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:03,960
About the application we submitted to the bureau

490
00:24:04,440 --> 00:24:05,319
regarding the venue...

491
00:24:05,960 --> 00:24:06,400
How's it going?

492
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:09,160
It's not... It's still...

493
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:10,160
well, you know...

494
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:11,720
we're having meetings to review it.

495
00:24:12,119 --> 00:24:12,599
Reviewing it.

496
00:24:13,119 --> 00:24:14,680
Soon. It should be resolved.

497
00:24:14,799 --> 00:24:16,160
It's been so long, it has to be resolved.

498
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:17,599
We're really getting anxious now.

499
00:24:17,759 --> 00:24:18,039
Yeah.

500
00:24:18,359 --> 00:24:19,559
The provincial competition is starting.

501
00:24:19,559 --> 00:24:20,799
Right, right, right.

502
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,319
This... This is quite tough.

503
00:24:23,559 --> 00:24:24,559
Since you're at the bureau,

504
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:27,200
when you see Chief Guo...

505
00:24:27,440 --> 00:24:28,359
Don't worry.

506
00:24:28,799 --> 00:24:29,680
Commissar, don't worry.

507
00:24:30,079 --> 00:24:31,119
When I see the Director,

508
00:24:31,279 --> 00:24:32,680
I'll definitely put in a good word for you.

509
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:33,240
Thank you, thank you.

510
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:33,960
It has to be resolved.

511
00:24:34,039 --> 00:24:35,559
The grassroots... The grassroots work,

512
00:24:35,559 --> 00:24:36,640
the comrades work very hard.

513
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:37,119
Yes, yes, yes.

514
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:38,920
Provide a better office environment, right?

515
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:39,839
And the training grounds,

516
00:24:40,319 --> 00:24:41,359
this is what we should do, right?

517
00:24:42,039 --> 00:24:43,240
The key is, we also want to

518
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:44,200
Yes, yes, yes.

519
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:45,960
Right, right, right.

520
00:24:46,079 --> 00:24:46,880
win some honor.

521
00:24:58,079 --> 00:25:00,480
You SWAT officers are part of the police too.

522
00:25:01,519 --> 00:25:03,599
Taking part in this Police Open Day...

523
00:25:04,319 --> 00:25:04,720
What's wrong with it?

524
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:07,039
We have absolutely no problem cooperating.

525
00:25:08,119 --> 00:25:09,359
But these kinds of performance tasks in the future...

526
00:25:09,359 --> 00:25:10,160
can we have fewer of them?

527
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:11,640
We're SWAT.

528
00:25:12,119 --> 00:25:12,960
Not actors.

529
00:25:21,599 --> 00:25:23,480
Did you come all the way here just for this?

530
00:25:24,559 --> 00:25:25,079
There's something else.

531
00:25:26,240 --> 00:25:26,519
Go ahead.

532
00:25:27,279 --> 00:25:28,519
The training ground you promised us...

533
00:25:28,519 --> 00:25:29,559
when will it be ready?

534
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:32,200
We're gearing up for the provincials soon.

535
00:25:32,559 --> 00:25:33,440
We need a place to train.

536
00:25:35,279 --> 00:25:36,640
Our municipal bureau's training ground...

537
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:37,079
can't you use that?

538
00:25:37,079 --> 00:25:38,839
That ground is fine for other units.

539
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:41,960
Our SWAT team's training content...

540
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:42,759
is different from theirs.

541
00:25:44,359 --> 00:25:46,680
We do rappelling, climbing, EOD, and assaults.

542
00:25:47,319 --> 00:25:49,000
I have to borrow space from the fire dept.

543
00:25:51,640 --> 00:25:52,720
When the team was first formed,

544
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:54,160
you put us in an elementary school,

545
00:25:54,799 --> 00:25:56,119
saying it was temporary.

546
00:25:57,079 --> 00:25:58,119
We've been there for eight years.

547
00:25:59,480 --> 00:26:00,720
No matter how tough the living conditions are,

548
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:01,880
we can deal with it.

549
00:26:01,880 --> 00:26:03,079
But the training ground

550
00:26:03,400 --> 00:26:04,079
and its quality

551
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:05,279
must be guaranteed.

552
00:26:06,359 --> 00:26:07,640
Because we charge at the front,

553
00:26:08,119 --> 00:26:09,599
doing things others can't do.

554
00:26:10,079 --> 00:26:10,759
Right, Chief Guo?

555
00:26:11,880 --> 00:26:12,119
Right.

556
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:13,519
Anything else?

557
00:26:13,519 --> 00:26:13,920
Yes.

558
00:26:15,039 --> 00:26:16,640
It's about personnel secondments.

559
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,160
Since they're borrowed,

560
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,359
shouldn't they be returned?

561
00:26:22,759 --> 00:26:24,200
They borrowed our men,

562
00:26:24,759 --> 00:26:25,960
so what's the deal with not returning them?

563
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:27,640
Are you finished?

564
00:26:28,319 --> 00:26:28,680
I'm finished.

565
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:30,240
It's my turn to speak.

566
00:26:32,079 --> 00:26:32,920
Liao Bufan, let me ask you.

567
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:35,359
What does SWAT mean?

568
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,440
The last line of defense for this city.

569
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:41,480
Since you know the importance of SWAT,

570
00:26:43,279 --> 00:26:45,119
then you have a problem with your attitude.

571
00:26:47,079 --> 00:26:48,680
Whether it's SWAT or any other unit,

572
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:51,480
we are all here to serve the people,

573
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:54,400
and to ensure the safety of their lives

574
00:26:54,400 --> 00:26:55,519
and their property.

575
00:26:55,519 --> 00:26:55,880
Right?

576
00:26:57,640 --> 00:26:59,079
You treat the Police Open Day

577
00:26:59,759 --> 00:27:00,799
as a mere performance.

578
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:03,079
That's a flaw in your understanding.

579
00:27:04,240 --> 00:27:05,240
I always tell you,

580
00:27:06,279 --> 00:27:08,400
we must never forget who we are.

581
00:27:09,119 --> 00:27:11,519
Never forget why we joined the force.

582
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:18,119
As for the training ground,

583
00:27:18,359 --> 00:27:20,000
I've been requesting it from the city leaders.

584
00:27:21,039 --> 00:27:22,160
But whether it'll be approved,

585
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:24,039
and when it'll be approved,

586
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:26,440
is not up to me.

587
00:27:27,720 --> 00:27:28,759
I hope you understand.

588
00:27:29,920 --> 00:27:31,039
We've been understanding for eight years.

589
00:27:31,039 --> 00:27:32,119
Of course I know it's been eight years.

590
00:27:32,319 --> 00:27:33,440
Eight years and three months, to be exact.

591
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:35,960
And regarding the secondments,

592
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:38,039
think about it.

593
00:27:39,079 --> 00:27:40,680
Do the other units refuse to return them,

594
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:42,680
or do our men not want to come back?

595
00:27:43,519 --> 00:27:45,119
Why don't you use your brain and think about it?

596
00:27:45,119 --> 00:27:45,880
I know why.

597
00:27:46,160 --> 00:27:46,880
Tell me why.

598
00:27:47,599 --> 00:27:49,599
Our SWAT team doesn't have investigative powers.

599
00:27:50,359 --> 00:27:51,279
Only execution powers.

600
00:27:52,519 --> 00:27:53,599
In all cases,

601
00:27:53,680 --> 00:27:54,839
we're just providing support.

602
00:27:55,759 --> 00:27:57,400
We charge forward into the most dangerous situations.

603
00:27:58,200 --> 00:28:00,359
We rarely get awards or commendations.

604
00:28:01,599 --> 00:28:03,880
Local stations earn more merits than us.

605
00:28:05,519 --> 00:28:06,720
The brothers feel there's nothing to look forward to.

606
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:07,319
Brothers?

607
00:28:08,359 --> 00:28:08,920
What brothers?

608
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:10,240
Liao Bufan.

609
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:12,039
Any team

610
00:28:12,519 --> 00:28:13,559
that relies only on brotherly loyalty

611
00:28:13,759 --> 00:28:15,000
is destined to fall apart.

612
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:22,079
Xiao Liao.

613
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:25,160
Your SWAT detachment is full of energy.

614
00:28:25,240 --> 00:28:26,240
You've trained them well.

615
00:28:26,519 --> 00:28:27,720
I can see that.

616
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:30,720
But you can't just rely on muscle.

617
00:28:31,079 --> 00:28:32,000
What good are big arms?

618
00:28:32,160 --> 00:28:33,119
What good is brute strength?

619
00:28:35,519 --> 00:28:37,000
Try using your brain sometimes.

620
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:41,680
Look at this.

621
00:28:43,279 --> 00:28:44,319
For two consecutive quarters,

622
00:28:44,880 --> 00:28:46,400
you've ranked dead last in political work.

623
00:28:47,279 --> 00:28:48,000
How do you explain this?

624
00:28:49,200 --> 00:28:50,359
More than one person has told me

625
00:28:51,319 --> 00:28:52,119
that your SWAT detachment

626
00:28:52,680 --> 00:28:53,920
operates like a dictatorship.

627
00:28:54,480 --> 00:28:56,160
The officers act like a fraternity.

628
00:28:58,759 --> 00:29:00,359
Are your political meetings held on time?

629
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:07,279
Go back

630
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:09,200
and work with Commissar Lu Zhong

631
00:29:09,759 --> 00:29:11,240
to come up with a rectification plan.

632
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:13,119
Submit it to me next week.

633
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:14,759
Yes, Chief Guo.

634
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:15,359
Louder.

635
00:29:15,559 --> 00:29:16,400
Yes, Chief Guo!

636
00:29:18,359 --> 00:29:19,039
Pathetic.

637
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:33,599
It's just a performance!

638
00:29:33,599 --> 00:29:34,240
You're actually hitting hard!

639
00:29:43,039 --> 00:29:44,319
Get a shot of that kid's smiling face. The kid.

640
00:29:44,319 --> 00:29:46,119
Capture... capture that smiling face. Capture his smile.

641
00:29:47,839 --> 00:29:48,720
Keep it up!

642
00:29:51,279 --> 00:29:51,839
Salute!

643
00:29:52,799 --> 00:29:54,319
The police open day is a huge success.

644
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:55,559
Thank you for your support, Commissar.

645
00:29:56,039 --> 00:29:57,400
Chief Zhao, don't mention it.

646
00:29:57,519 --> 00:29:58,920
It's the least we could do.

647
00:29:59,319 --> 00:30:00,519
My regards to the comrades.

648
00:30:00,759 --> 00:30:01,519
Alright, I'll be going now.

649
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:02,640
Alright, take care.

650
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:02,920
Okay.

651
00:30:04,200 --> 00:30:05,680
Let us know if you need anything.

652
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:05,960
Will do.

653
00:30:08,599 --> 00:30:09,839
Everyone, hurry up.

654
00:30:10,519 --> 00:30:10,839
Yunsheng.

655
00:30:12,599 --> 00:30:12,880
Commissar.

656
00:30:12,880 --> 00:30:13,160
Well...

657
00:30:14,039 --> 00:30:15,440
Your matter is almost settled.

658
00:30:16,519 --> 00:30:17,359
Once it's confirmed,

659
00:30:17,519 --> 00:30:18,079
I'll talk to Captain Liao.

660
00:30:18,519 --> 00:30:19,160
Thank you, Commissar.

661
00:30:20,440 --> 00:30:22,079
We fought together, no need for thanks.

662
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:23,720
Keep up the good work from now on.

663
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:24,039
Yes, sir.

664
00:30:24,359 --> 00:30:24,680
Go on.

665
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:27,000
Everyone, hurry up.

666
00:30:27,119 --> 00:30:27,920
Be quick but orderly.

667
00:30:28,799 --> 00:30:30,000
Hey there, you two girls.

668
00:30:30,079 --> 00:30:30,960
Haven't you filmed enough?

669
00:30:30,960 --> 00:30:31,960
I saw you film a lot during rehearsal.

670
00:30:31,960 --> 00:30:32,920
Come on, let's take one together.

671
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:33,799
Let's record a video.

672
00:30:33,799 --> 00:30:34,359
Come on, come here.

673
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:35,559
Recording a video.

674
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:36,160
Okay.

675
00:30:38,480 --> 00:30:39,559
Three, two, one, start!

676
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:40,720
Cheese!

677
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:42,559
Cheese!

678
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:44,200
Alright.

679
00:30:44,279 --> 00:30:44,839
Well then, ladies.

680
00:30:44,839 --> 00:30:46,200
We have things to do back at the station.

681
00:30:46,599 --> 00:30:47,440
That's all for today.

682
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:48,160
Hurry up!

683
00:30:48,240 --> 00:30:48,359
Okay.

684
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:50,079
Come on, hurry up.

685
00:30:50,079 --> 00:30:50,559
Officer!

686
00:30:50,720 --> 00:30:52,240
Can I add you on WeChat?

687
00:30:52,519 --> 00:30:53,240
Sorry, I can't.

688
00:30:55,200 --> 00:30:57,279
Officer, let's add each other on WeChat then.

689
00:30:57,400 --> 00:30:57,839
Come on, let me add you.

690
00:30:59,200 --> 00:30:59,759
Great!

691
00:31:02,279 --> 00:31:02,960
Send me the video later.

692
00:31:04,799 --> 00:31:05,319
Thank you, Officer.

693
00:31:09,200 --> 00:31:10,519
15 to 20 grams of brown sugar.

694
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:12,039
Adjust based on blood sugar levels.

695
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:14,119
One egg, 600 milliliters of water.

696
00:31:14,319 --> 00:31:16,240
Stage one: simmer to extract the medicine.

697
00:31:16,400 --> 00:31:19,039
Put astragalus, ginger, and red dates in a clay pot.

698
00:31:19,039 --> 00:31:20,319
Add 600 milliliters of cold water.

699
00:31:20,319 --> 00:31:20,759
Chief Tan.

700
00:31:20,759 --> 00:31:22,039
Bring to a boil, then reduce to low heat.

701
00:31:22,039 --> 00:31:23,000
Simmer for 20 minutes.

702
00:31:23,319 --> 00:31:23,880
To allow the astragalus...

703
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:25,519
Chief Tan, you haven't left work yet?

704
00:31:26,240 --> 00:31:28,799
How did the police open day go?

705
00:31:28,960 --> 00:31:30,039
Extremely successful.

706
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:32,000
The atmosphere was very enthusiastic.

707
00:31:32,200 --> 00:31:34,079
Chief Zhao praised you all the way back.

708
00:31:34,680 --> 00:31:36,200
He said you came up with a great idea.

709
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:39,079
Publicity really looked good this time.

710
00:31:41,920 --> 00:31:43,240
Did the guys from the SWAT detachment...

711
00:31:44,559 --> 00:31:45,079
cooperate?

712
00:31:47,519 --> 00:31:49,160
Chief Zhao went straight to Commissar Lu.

713
00:31:50,680 --> 00:31:51,640
Explained the situation.

714
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:53,160
And the SWAT team sent people over.

715
00:31:54,039 --> 00:31:56,319
Moreover, they were all top-notch.

716
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:04,160
I'm going to the restroom.

717
00:32:16,839 --> 00:32:17,720
We got careless

718
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:24,799
Chief Guo

719
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:28,359
I have a rough little idea

720
00:32:28,359 --> 00:32:29,240
I'd like to report to you

721
00:32:29,599 --> 00:32:31,359
How rough? Let's hear it

722
00:32:31,960 --> 00:32:32,640
On Friday,

723
00:32:32,799 --> 00:32:35,240
the city is holding an investment forum

724
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:37,200
City leaders will attend

725
00:32:37,359 --> 00:32:38,880
I hear there'll be many foreign investors

726
00:32:39,359 --> 00:32:39,559
Really?

727
00:32:39,880 --> 00:32:41,200
So I was wondering

728
00:32:41,720 --> 00:32:44,279
if we should send our SWAT team on duty

729
00:32:45,240 --> 00:32:45,839
First,

730
00:32:46,519 --> 00:32:48,279
it shows we take it seriously

731
00:32:48,920 --> 00:32:49,440
Second,

732
00:32:50,519 --> 00:32:52,119
there'll be a big crowd that day

733
00:32:52,759 --> 00:32:53,720
With SWAT there,

734
00:32:55,200 --> 00:32:56,240
security will be more solid

735
00:32:56,960 --> 00:32:57,519
Third,

736
00:32:57,839 --> 00:32:59,480
let the city leaders and investors

737
00:32:59,480 --> 00:33:02,000
see what our SWAT team can do

738
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:03,799
It's good publicity for us too

739
00:33:04,799 --> 00:33:06,519
That sounds pretty well thought out

740
00:33:06,920 --> 00:33:08,640
Coordinate it based on your idea, then

741
00:33:09,119 --> 00:33:09,400
Yes, sir

742
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:13,640
By the way, today's Police Open Day...

743
00:33:14,640 --> 00:33:16,359
How do you think it went?

744
00:33:17,519 --> 00:33:18,720
Chief Guo, Chief Guo

745
00:33:23,799 --> 00:33:24,720
I heard

746
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:25,920
it went pretty well

747
00:33:26,519 --> 00:33:27,279
That's good

748
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:31,519
Chief Zhao came to me before

749
00:33:32,680 --> 00:33:35,599
about which police unit would fit best

750
00:33:36,200 --> 00:33:39,240
After thinking it over, SWAT seemed best

751
00:33:40,319 --> 00:33:41,160
People haven't seen them before

752
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:42,079
It feels fresh

753
00:33:42,880 --> 00:33:44,200
and publicity gets a strong angle

754
00:33:45,240 --> 00:33:45,640
Tan Yan

755
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:48,559
The way you look at things now

756
00:33:48,880 --> 00:33:49,680
is getting more and more well-rounded

757
00:33:50,240 --> 00:33:51,559
That's only under your leadership

758
00:33:51,680 --> 00:33:53,079
that I've been able to grow so fast

759
00:33:56,519 --> 00:33:57,599
Director Gu has retired too

760
00:33:58,319 --> 00:34:00,759
so I must work even harder and stay alert

761
00:34:00,759 --> 00:34:02,440
to hold the line in publicity work

762
00:34:03,079 --> 00:34:04,079
Time really flies, doesn't it?

763
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:06,599
Old Gu, just like that,

764
00:34:08,400 --> 00:34:09,760
has been retired for a while now, right?

765
00:34:10,519 --> 00:34:11,280
Over two months

766
00:34:13,320 --> 00:34:14,719
The Publicity Division's work

767
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:17,239
needs someone to take charge of it properly

768
00:34:22,199 --> 00:34:22,480
We're here

769
00:34:23,679 --> 00:34:24,079
You go on up

770
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:24,840
I'll walk you up

771
00:34:24,840 --> 00:34:25,400
No need to walk me

772
00:34:44,239 --> 00:34:45,760
This one's red. We can eat this one.

773
00:34:45,920 --> 00:34:46,159
Don't touch.

774
00:34:46,719 --> 00:34:47,760
This crop didn't yield much.

775
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:48,800
Leave some for the rest of the guys.

776
00:34:57,760 --> 00:34:59,360
This crappy place.

777
00:35:01,719 --> 00:35:02,719
Nothing grows well here.

778
00:35:07,599 --> 00:35:09,320
From what Chief Guo was saying,

779
00:35:10,119 --> 00:35:11,079
before the big competition,

780
00:35:11,440 --> 00:35:13,039
a training ground is out of the question.

781
00:35:16,360 --> 00:35:17,360
I'm really out of ideas this time.

782
00:35:19,239 --> 00:35:20,880
The location isn't set in stone yet, right?

783
00:35:22,519 --> 00:35:23,599
We'll cross that bridge when we come to it.

784
00:35:23,599 --> 00:35:24,719
You're not worried?

785
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:25,840
Don't you want to place?

786
00:35:27,119 --> 00:35:27,760
I am worried.

787
00:35:28,440 --> 00:35:30,199
But if worrying could solve problems,

788
00:35:30,559 --> 00:35:32,079
I'd worry a thousand times a day.

789
00:35:35,559 --> 00:35:36,559
There are some things

790
00:35:37,239 --> 00:35:38,039
you can only keep to yourself.

791
00:35:39,400 --> 00:35:41,079
Saying them out loud doesn't solve anything,

792
00:35:41,280 --> 00:35:42,320
and it just ruins everyone's morale.

793
00:35:43,400 --> 00:35:44,280
To be honest,

794
00:35:44,519 --> 00:35:46,679
whenever I watch those videos, I wonder...

795
00:35:48,599 --> 00:35:50,000
what if one day,

796
00:35:51,199 --> 00:35:52,360
we could also stand on that podium?

797
00:35:53,119 --> 00:35:53,639
What would that feel like?

798
00:35:55,760 --> 00:35:57,760
Sometimes I fall asleep thinking about it.

799
00:35:58,599 --> 00:35:58,920
I gotta say,

800
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:01,079
in my dreams,

801
00:36:02,079 --> 00:36:02,760
I actually stood up there.

802
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,119
On the highest spot.

803
00:36:05,239 --> 00:36:06,760
So, the saying is true...

804
00:36:07,239 --> 00:36:09,280
When you're tired or stressed, just go to sleep.

805
00:36:09,440 --> 00:36:10,559
You can have everything in your dreams.

806
00:36:11,400 --> 00:36:13,039
Then you better wake up.

807
00:36:15,559 --> 00:36:16,519
These tomatoes are actually pretty good.

808
00:36:16,639 --> 00:36:17,079
Not bad.

809
00:36:17,199 --> 00:36:18,840
I grew them myself, little by little.

810
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:22,239
Old Liao,

811
00:36:23,199 --> 00:36:25,360
Based on our current circumstances,

812
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:26,920
there are indeed many difficulties.

813
00:36:27,760 --> 00:36:28,280
But think about it.

814
00:36:30,679 --> 00:36:31,880
The Long March back then

815
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:33,400
was difficult. The Korean War was too.

816
00:36:34,639 --> 00:36:35,119
Right.

817
00:36:35,719 --> 00:36:36,920
But didn't we win in the end?

818
00:36:37,760 --> 00:36:38,119
Why?

819
00:36:39,079 --> 00:36:41,159
Because the red flag in everyone's hearts

820
00:36:41,159 --> 00:36:42,199
never fell.

821
00:36:43,480 --> 00:36:45,119
Today, let's set a small goal.

822
00:36:45,800 --> 00:36:46,719
No matter how great the difficulties are,

823
00:36:47,679 --> 00:36:48,840
in this year's provincial competition,

824
00:36:48,960 --> 00:36:49,840
at the very least,

825
00:36:50,119 --> 00:36:51,000
we'll take first place in the province.

826
00:36:51,199 --> 00:36:51,719
It's settled.

827
00:36:53,719 --> 00:36:54,360
Second place won't do?

828
00:36:58,079 --> 00:36:58,519
No.

829
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:00,039
We have to be first.

830
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:02,239
First place stands the highest.

831
00:37:13,800 --> 00:37:17,159
Yesterday I filmed Lao Na's artifact bust.

832
00:37:18,320 --> 00:37:19,159
When I got there,

833
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:21,480
they had already caught everyone.

834
00:37:23,559 --> 00:37:25,760
I insisted on shooting some extra footage.

835
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:28,840
Lao Na was pretty accommodating.

836
00:37:30,280 --> 00:37:32,119
He let me shoot some footage of vehicle inspections.

837
00:37:34,760 --> 00:37:35,239
The water temperature is good.

838
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:42,840
So I organized the crew to shoot.

839
00:37:44,679 --> 00:37:46,960
When we were shooting the fourth or fifth car,

840
00:37:47,119 --> 00:37:47,880
Get to the point.

841
00:37:49,679 --> 00:37:51,239
Relying on my years of

842
00:37:52,559 --> 00:37:53,920
professional judgment,

843
00:37:54,079 --> 00:37:55,920
I saw a guy through the lens

844
00:37:55,920 --> 00:37:56,480
looking suspicious.

845
00:37:56,840 --> 00:37:58,280
I sprinted right out there.

846
00:37:58,960 --> 00:38:00,000
Lao Na was quick to react too.

847
00:38:01,599 --> 00:38:02,559
I yelled out,

848
00:38:03,280 --> 00:38:05,079
"Pin down the guy in the bucket hat!"

849
00:38:05,280 --> 00:38:05,800
"Pin him down!"

850
00:38:10,039 --> 00:38:10,559
And guess what?

851
00:38:12,079 --> 00:38:13,239
Two kilograms of drugs.

852
00:38:13,840 --> 00:38:15,039
Seized on the spot.

853
00:38:17,199 --> 00:38:18,239
You rushed in first?

854
00:38:19,679 --> 00:38:20,320
I couldn't hold back.

855
00:38:22,199 --> 00:38:24,000
How could Lao Na let you rush in first?

856
00:38:24,840 --> 00:38:25,880
This guy is unbelievable.

857
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:26,920
Letting you rush in first.

858
00:38:27,280 --> 00:38:27,920
I'm going to call him.

859
00:38:29,039 --> 00:38:29,679
Don't call him.

860
00:38:30,159 --> 00:38:31,280
He's interrogating him right now.

861
00:38:33,400 --> 00:38:35,559
Word is spreading all over the City Bureau

862
00:38:35,679 --> 00:38:37,559
that a guy with a camera can also catch

863
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:38,599
a drug dealer.

864
00:38:49,159 --> 00:38:50,480
I heard the police open house

865
00:38:50,840 --> 00:38:51,559
went really well.

866
00:38:53,320 --> 00:38:54,760
All the credit goes to Lao Zhao.

867
00:38:57,199 --> 00:38:59,559
I heard Qin Juan got transferred to Immigration.

868
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:00,719
Her position is open now.

869
00:39:01,679 --> 00:39:02,480
This opportunity...

870
00:39:02,719 --> 00:39:03,719
you can't let it go to waste.

871
00:39:06,039 --> 00:39:07,519
I'm not doing this for myself.

872
00:39:11,199 --> 00:39:11,800
We'll talk about it later.

873
00:39:11,920 --> 00:39:12,960
Don't put it off.

874
00:39:13,800 --> 00:39:15,719
It's a great opportunity. Listen to me.

875
00:39:16,320 --> 00:39:17,360
Invite her out.

876
00:39:19,920 --> 00:39:20,639
Alright, I'll listen to you.

877
00:39:21,440 --> 00:39:22,400
You have to listen to me.

878
00:39:22,480 --> 00:39:24,239
When I transferred from Luteng to Hongye,

879
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:25,800
wasn't I listening to you?

880
00:39:27,840 --> 00:39:29,199
That wasn't listening to me.

881
00:39:30,639 --> 00:39:31,800
That was listening to love.

882
00:39:43,119 --> 00:39:43,920
Pass me the towel.

883
00:39:44,480 --> 00:39:46,480
Soak a bit longer to relax.

884
00:39:46,480 --> 00:39:47,639
Quick, lie back down.

885
00:39:48,599 --> 00:39:49,639
I'll go get you some water.

886
00:39:56,199 --> 00:39:58,639
Didn't we agree?

887
00:40:01,480 --> 00:40:04,039
This station is just a stepping stone.

888
00:40:05,239 --> 00:40:07,000
Don't forget our end goal.

889
00:40:07,639 --> 00:40:08,719
Seize the opportunity,

890
00:40:09,960 --> 00:40:11,400
and take another step forward.

891
00:40:15,239 --> 00:40:16,480
Think about all these years.

892
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:17,599
Haven't we always...

893
00:41:00,280 --> 00:41:01,320
What's the rush?

894
00:41:01,559 --> 00:41:03,280
I'm on my way.

895
00:41:07,760 --> 00:41:09,559
Wait, your version of the drug bust

896
00:41:10,199 --> 00:41:11,960
is different from what Lao Tan told me.

897
00:41:12,639 --> 00:41:13,360
How about you two go to that room

898
00:41:13,360 --> 00:41:14,480
and get your stories straight first?

899
00:41:15,519 --> 00:41:16,679
What's your version?

900
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:21,480
The version isn't important.

901
00:41:22,039 --> 00:41:24,480
What matters is that due to my persistence,

902
00:41:24,679 --> 00:41:25,800
he cracked this major case.

903
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:27,239
So impressive.

904
00:41:27,239 --> 00:41:28,559
Can't argue with that.

905
00:41:28,840 --> 00:41:30,480
Yesterday's success was all Lao Tan's doing.

906
00:41:33,079 --> 00:41:33,639
I'm telling you,

907
00:41:34,239 --> 00:41:34,679
Lao Tan,

908
00:41:35,199 --> 00:41:35,840
don't you feel like

909
00:41:36,320 --> 00:41:37,679
God is on your side?

910
00:41:38,639 --> 00:41:40,079
If this investment conference goes well,

911
00:41:40,559 --> 00:41:42,199
the position of Publicity Director...

912
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:44,119
I think...

913
00:41:45,159 --> 00:41:46,079
it's still a long shot.

914
00:41:46,840 --> 00:41:47,840
That's right, that's right.

915
00:41:48,400 --> 00:41:49,559
Lao Zhao is still ahead of him.

916
00:41:49,880 --> 00:41:51,039
He has the seniority.

917
00:41:52,039 --> 00:41:53,199
Seniority is important,

918
00:41:53,519 --> 00:41:55,960
but aren't they pushing for younger cadres?

919
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:57,360
And you made Lao Guo look so good,

920
00:41:57,360 --> 00:41:58,440
he'll definitely back you.

921
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:00,440
Even though...

922
00:42:00,840 --> 00:42:02,559
this whole "younger cadres" thing

923
00:42:03,079 --> 00:42:04,119
has nothing to do with you,

924
00:42:04,960 --> 00:42:05,519
but still,

925
00:42:06,239 --> 00:42:07,119
congratulations are in order.

926
00:42:07,880 --> 00:42:09,519
May the investment conference go smoothly.

927
00:42:10,679 --> 00:42:12,360
Deputy Director Tan, come on.

928
00:42:12,840 --> 00:42:13,519
Come on, Deputy Director Tan.

929
00:42:14,360 --> 00:42:14,679
Cheers.

930
00:42:14,800 --> 00:42:15,360
Let's toast with tea instead of alcohol.

931
00:42:16,159 --> 00:42:16,480
Congratulations!

932
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:17,400
Thanks for the good wishes.

933
00:42:34,760 --> 00:42:35,239
Really?

934
00:42:36,079 --> 00:42:36,920
Okay, okay.

935
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:43,280
We got something.

936
00:42:45,199 --> 00:42:47,039
A buddy of mine says he's seen this guy.

937
00:42:47,679 --> 00:42:49,360
But he has a condition.

938
00:42:50,280 --> 00:42:50,599
Let's hear it.

939
00:42:51,280 --> 00:42:52,000
Well, he...

940
00:42:52,000 --> 00:42:53,559
...is also into this stuff.

941
00:42:54,960 --> 00:42:56,039
What a coincidence, huh?

942
00:43:02,039 --> 00:43:02,519
Fine.

943
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:14,400
Did you see anything when it happened?

944
00:43:14,639 --> 00:43:17,320
There was someone in the window.

945
00:43:17,320 --> 00:43:18,280
What are you doing here?

946
00:43:18,480 --> 00:43:19,119
I live next door.

947
00:43:22,880 --> 00:43:24,159
At the scene of Lu Zhong's death...

948
00:43:24,159 --> 00:43:26,280
...there were at least three suspects.

949
00:43:26,280 --> 00:43:27,599
That bag of powder on the ground...

950
00:43:27,599 --> 00:43:28,760
...is highly suspicious.

951
00:43:28,760 --> 00:43:30,480
Set up the 215 Special Task Force.

952
00:43:30,480 --> 00:43:32,920
I want the killer pinned down in Hongye.

953
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:35,119
Where's my gun?
